{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"03/11/2026 13:27:28","profile":{"player_id":"118077","last_updated":"03/11/2026 13:27","fullname":"Oliver John Peake","short_display_name":"O Peake","name":"Oliver Peake","gender":"M","dob":"11/09/2006","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Australia","nationality_id":"1","nationality":"Australia","nationality_short_code":"AUS","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"1","text":"Batsman","role":"Batter"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"7","text":"Off break"},"writeup":"<p>Calm under pressure and remarkably mature beyond his years, Oliver Peake has rapidly emerged as one of Australia&rsquo;s most exciting young batting prospects, earning attention for his elegant strokeplay, composure and ability to deliver in big moments.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nBorn in Geelong, Victoria, Peake comes from a strong cricketing background, with his father Clinton Peake having also represented Victoria and captained Australia at Under-19 level. A left-handed batter with a compact technique and natural game awareness, Oliver rose through Victoria&rsquo;s pathway system and made headlines during the 2024 ICC Under-19 World Cup in South Africa. Initially named as a travelling reserve, he forced his way into the playing XI after an injury in the squad and made an immediate impact, scoring a crucial 49 against Pakistan in the semi-final before producing an unbeaten 46 in the final against India to help Australia lift the title.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nHis rise in domestic cricket was equally impressive. Peake made his Sheffield Shield debut for Victoria during the 2024/25 season and top-scored with 52 on debut against Western Australia at the WACA, showcasing his temperament in difficult conditions. He quickly established himself as one of Victoria&rsquo;s brightest young batters and was rewarded with a rookie state contract ahead of the 2025/26 season. By the age of 19, he had already crossed 500 First-class runs while also impressing in List A cricket with multiple half-centuries. His consistent performances also earned him Australia A selection in 2025, where he announced himself with an unbeaten 55 from just 38 balls against Sri Lanka A.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nIn franchise cricket, Peake broke through with Melbourne Renegades in the Big Bash League and quickly gained recognition for his fearless approach in pressure situations. One of his defining moments came during the 2025/26 BBL season when he smashed a last-ball six against Perth Scorchers to seal a dramatic chase, a knock that further elevated his reputation as a future Australian star. He finished the season with his maiden BBL half-century and continued to strengthen his white-ball credentials with mature middle-order performances.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nPeake also captained Australia at the 2026 ICC Under-19 World Cup, becoming the only returning member from the victorious 2024 squad. He led from the front throughout the tournament, including a brilliant century against West Indies in the Super Six stage and a fighting hundred against England in the semi-final. Widely regarded as one of the finest young batting talents in Australian cricket, his rapid progression through domestic, franchise and pathway cricket was further rewarded with a maiden call-up to Australia&rsquo;s ODI squad for the 2026 tour of Pakistan.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nPeake made his senior international debut in the 1st ODI against Pakistan, taking the next step in his progression from pathway cricket to the international stage. He also featured in the Global Super League 2026 campaign for San Francisco Unicorns, scoring 135 runs in their road to the final, gaining further experience in franchise cricket, before being included in Australia's ODI squad for the tours of Zimbabwe and South Africa. The selections underlined the faith in Peake as one of the country's emerging batting prospects and gave him further opportunities to develop his game at the highest level.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>","relation":[{"id":27796,"name":"Clinton Peake","relation":"Father","relation_id":1}],"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Australia"},{"id":"47","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Australia A"},{"id":"1137","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Victoria"},{"id":"1154","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"1","text":"Australia Under-19"},{"id":"1265","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Melbourne Renegades"},{"id":"1551","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Prime Ministers XI"},{"id":"3212","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Melbourne Renegades Academy"},{"id":"3842","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"San Francisco Unicorns"},{"id":"4971","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Melbourne Red Fury"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"2","comp_type":"ODI International - m","match_id":"270975","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/matches/270975/pakistan-vs-australia","series_id":"15565","series_name":"Australia in Pakistan, 3 ODI Series, 2026","match_date":"30/05/2026","for":{"id":"1","text":"Australia","short_name":"AUS"},"vs":{"id":"6","text":"Pakistan","short_name":"PAK"},"venue":{"id":"134","text":"Rawalpindi Cricket Stadium, Rawalpindi"},"batting":{"runs":"7","balls_faced":"16","hundreds":"0","innings":[{"number":"1","runs":"7","balls_faced":"16","hundreds":""}]},"bowling":{"wickets":"","runs_given":"","ball_bowled":"","economy":"","five_wk_hauls":"0","innings":[]},"fielding":{"catches":"0","stumpings":"0","run_outs":"0","innings":[]}},"international_last_match":{"comp_type_id":"2","comp_type":"ODI International - m","match_id":"269789","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/matches/269789/south-africa-vs-australia","series_i